title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: Summary
agents: windows
catalog: os/virtual
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check shows the name, the power state, the Hyper-V host and the
 generation of a virtual machine running on Microsoft Hyper-V.

 The monitoring state of each power state is configured with the rule
 "Hyper-V VM summary". By default the check is {OK} if the VM is running
 or saved, {WARN} if it is paused or starting and {CRIT} if it is off.
 Any other power state is {UNKNOWN}.

 By default the check is {WARN} if the VM is not a generation 2 VM. The
 expected generation and the state are configured in the same rule.

 The check is {WARN} if the power state, the host or the generation is
 missing in the agent output.

 The VM gets the host label {cmk/hyperv_object:vm}.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

discovery:
 One service is created on the piggyback host of each VM.
